17592186051029 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7b7f598a-21a7-593a-99a2-ef8e0258c820" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107604 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107604 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107604 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107604 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186540654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107604 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "caf9ab22-db76-5d02-b2ce-c710382a7b35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107606 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186563182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107606 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107606 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107606 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186563182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107606 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9fc6a2b7-5d2f-5c82-ae12-de24bf2f6659" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110351 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14854" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110351 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched below.\n\n![](images/e5/e5393f15ff154f1f4cc310791790db0fe0ad0d9faa076d10f3f6ec7b481de086.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110351 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "30974188-c734-5e99-a9ae-81d1a53b9105" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110351 #edb/ref 1074 "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-3+2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110352 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14857" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110352 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x-1)(x-5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "00575d99-28e6-59b7-b416-765808916fe5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110352 #edb/ref 1074 "From the equation $y=-(x-1)(x-5),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=1$ and $x_2=5.$\n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2} = \\dfrac{1+5}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110353 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110353 #edb/ref 1071 "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2)$ is $x=6.$ Find the value of $k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110353 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "405e0230-69cb-5679-bec0-13a69c722934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110353 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6,$ we will set our result equal to $6.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=k$ and $x_2=-2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k-2}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k-2}{2} & =6 \\\\ k-2 & =12 \\\\ k & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110373 #edb/ref 1069 "e-19740" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110373 #edb/ref 1071 "| **$x$** | $4$ | $12$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $9$ | $25$ | $9$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y = f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110373 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04877936-271e-5fcb-a1ea-aa39c52482b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110373 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=4$ and $x=20$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(4) = f(20) = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=4$ and $x=20.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabolas vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{4+20}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186541059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186541064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186541116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186563701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186563721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186563762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110725 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186541122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186541127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186563686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110726 #edb/r