ve shows a parabola. The $x$-coordinates of $A$ and $B$ are $-\\frac{8}{3}$ and $\\frac{11}{5},$ respectively.  Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola.\n\nThe axis of symmetry is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f8c9da4-4b17-554e-b183-7584d639d444" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110976 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given that the roots of the parabola are \n ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{11}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{11}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{40}{15}+\\frac{33}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{7}{30}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186107606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223695" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110978 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110978 #edb/ref 1071 "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x+5k)(3x-4k)$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{8}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8660b4e2-d758-5150-9ae4-48bf3487cb6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110978 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{8},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{1}{8}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=-(x+5k)(3x-4k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-5k$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{4k}{3}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-5k+\\frac{4k}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-\\frac{11k}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11k}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{8}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11k}{6} & =-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ -11k & =-\\frac{6}{8} \\\\ -11k & =-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ k & =\\frac{3}{44}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111692 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111692 #edb/ref 1061 502427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111692 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0bf344b4-5c54-585a-ab6e-16e5a8e551f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111692 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111693 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111694 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111693 #edb/ref 1061 502428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111693 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "362cf052-a4cb-519a-968e-bda8b81a4551" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111693 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111694 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111694 #edb/ref 1061 502432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111694 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7dec3f3-b123-50ec-a737-75e54a076282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111694 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111695 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111695 #edb/ref 1061 502435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111695 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd4bd192-4cdd-5f22-9524-55cd3e1d3ba8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111695 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111696 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111696 #edb/ref 1061 502439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111696 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b132072-c297-50ce-be49-d3a763e0a32f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111696 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111697 #edb/ref 1061 502440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111697 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7518575-386c-57e6-893c-6238e3cc01a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111697 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111821 #edb/ref 1064 "![](images/b2/b27906f92121928be444d3b7f616becbcc7a849e1313ef50accd8c8bfd718bfb.png)\n\nIf we know two points on a parabola with *identical* $y$-values, we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking an average of the two $x$-values. \n\nFor example, consider the parabola $y=f(x)$ above. Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=-3$ and $x=5$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(-3) = f(5) = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=-3$ and $x=5.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabola's vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{-3+5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $h=1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the vertex, and the axis of symmetry of the parabola is $x=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111821 #edb/ref 1065 13792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111821 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "23d4f6e0-c0a7-5551-bd88-80b3268a5b2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111821 #edb/ref 1067 "Extending the Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111921 #edb/ref 1064 "If a parabola has two roots, the axis of symmetry occurs precisely halfway between the roots of the parabola. Therefore, we can find the axis of symmetry of a parabola by finding the roots and then taking their average value. \n\nSo, if the roots are $x_1$ and $x_2,$ the **average of the roots formula** tells us that the axis of symmetry of the parabola is\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2}.\n$$\n\nFor example, let's consider the parabola \n\n$$\ny=(x+2)(x-4).\n$$\n\nWe have the roots $x_1=-2$ and $x_2=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{-2+4}{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x+2)(x-4)$ is $x=1,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ec/ec08bc1ba75082ac98bb6559b6c0ef8119fbf245f3c266710ce8c6a569fa8a02.png)"